invalid type: string "Condition: Pacemaker Rhythm\nDefinition: A rhythm driven by an artificial electronic pacemaker device.\nDiagnostic Criteria: Presence of pacemaker spikes.\nECG Characteristics: Sharp, vertical pacing spikes preceding the P wave (atrial pacing) or QRS complex (ventricular pacing).\nTypical Heart Rate: Usually fixed at a set rate (e.g., 60-70 bpm) or tracks atrial activity.\nh>